  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Library's copy addressed on top of box in green marker: Mrs. Leonard Brown, 7 Crescent Hill, Springfield, Massachusetts 01105 U.S.A. Abs. Helmut Rywelski, 5 Köln 74, Mengenicher Str. 24. This address is repeated with minor variations on bottom of box. Customs declaration form mounted on front describes contents as "Geschenk, present." It is signed "Beatrice v. Bodisco", dated "23.4.71", and stamped "Passed free, New York." The right side of the box has been stamped "Final notice" in black ink.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Special issue of 4th no. of Roth's periodical Poetrie. It consists of 21 envelopes of clear soft plastic, on both sides of which the text is printed. The envelopes contain urine, now largely dessicated (see Dieter Rot, books and graphics). The envelopes have 4 holes at their inner margins, through which they are bound into a clear plastic cover (unprinted) with 2 pieces of clear plastic tubing.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">P. [1], title. P. [2], "Zweiter Teil der Poeterei 1968" and small printed device. P. [3]-[37], text. P. [38], "London, 18. März 1968." P. [38] and [39], original drawings carried out with red and green marking pens; signed in green marker on p. [39]: D.R. 70. P. [41], colophon ("30 signierte und numerierte Exemplare erschinen bei Art Intermedia, Helmut Rywelski, Köln"); signed in black marker: Diter Rot 68.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In particleboard box (17 x 29 x 20 cm.), reinforced with metal brackets at sides and bottom edges. The lid was nailed in place.</subfield>
  </datafield>
